‎## Hypothesis
‎As digital life increases isolation and performance pressure, 
‎demand for anonymous, non-judgmental human connection will grow.
‎The winners will be platforms that own the trust infrastructure, not just the chat interface.
‎
‎## Risk Map
‎**Who bears failure?** Listener burnout, ethical breaches, liability
‎**Who absorbs shocks?** Platform if trust is broken
‎**Who has liquidity?** Platform controls payout + reputation
‎**Who can exit?** Users with data/portability concerns
